All work is complete. Here's a summary of what was delivered:

**Movement and Positioning Rules (300-series)** — `Game Design Document/Gameplay Rules/Movement and Positioning Rules.md`

Six major sections covering:

1. **300 Battlefield Geometry** — Coordinate system (continuous x,y), default 200×100 dimensions, Euclidean distance formula, visual grid (1/3/6-unit zoom levels), boundary rules
2. **310 Movement** — Path vs displacement distinction, movement speed summary table, obstruction/pathfinding, collision with 1-DU separation, four invalid position types
3. **320 Unit Footprint & Model Cohesion** — Rectangular footprint, 1-DU Model diameter, 2-DU Cohesion Distance, default formations (5-file Infantry, 3-file Vehicle)
4. **330 Facing & Pivoting** — Angle in degrees clockwise from north, pivot cost formula proportional to angle and footprint size, free pivot on stationary Orders, automatic facing on movement
5. **340 Deployment & Reinforcements** — Default Deployment Zones codified, No Man's Land, Reinforcement Edge entry procedure, Vanguard and Pre-Engagement Moves
6. **350 Movement Restrictions** — Partial movement, Endurance/Morale/Melee constraints, movement does not provoke attacks

All cross-references verified against Battle Rules (100-series) and Entity System Rules (200-series). Includes 16 glossary entries, implementation state requirements, and pathfinding recommendations.

